        {"h2_html": "Fast, professional scheduling is what earns the <em>next agent referral</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">To a real estate agent, you are only as good as how easily their client can get on your schedule. Agents live and die by deadlines, and an inspector who answers, books quickly, and delivers a clean report the same day makes the agent look organized and reliable in front of their client, which is the whole reason an agent refers anyone at all. An inspector who is hard to reach, even once, at the wrong moment, is a risk the agent quietly stops taking, and they rarely tell you why. The phone is where that reputation is built or broken, long before you ever walk up to the house.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">That is why a single relationship is worth protecting. An agent who trusts you does not send one client, they send every buyer they represent for years, and they mention your name to the other agents in their office. One call answered well can be the beginning of that kind of steady referral stream, and one call missed at the wrong time can quietly end it. The receptionist makes sure the first thing a new agent hears is a calm, professional pickup that gets the inspection booked around their deadline, not a voicemail greeting they have to chase while their client waits on an answer.</p>'},
