        {"h2_html": "Your agent referrals are the whole business, and they slip through <em>follow-up</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Most home inspectors do not have a demand problem. They have a follow-up problem. The referral relationship with real estate agents is the entire lifeblood of an inspection business, because an agent who trusts you does not send one client, they send every buyer they represent, year after year. But those relationships are quietly maintained, not automatic. An agent uses you twice, you get slammed with a full week of inspections, you never circle back, and the third deal goes to the inspector who happened to stay in touch. Nothing went wrong. You just got busy, which is the one thing every good inspector always is.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">A CRM keeps every agent, every past client, and every open quote in one place and follows up for you, on a schedule you set, whether or not you remember. The agent who has not called in a while gets a light, genuine check-in before they drift to someone else. The buyer who asked for a price and went quiet hears from you again. The relationships and quotes you already earned stop slipping away between inspections and start turning back into booked work, without you keeping a running list in your head.</p>'},
